    "https://www.avondale.edu.au/job/learning-and-teaching-support-officer/": {
      "title": "Learning and Teaching Support Officer",
      "description": "Learning and Teaching Support Officer - Avondale University Current Students Staff Library Alumni News & Events HOME CURRENT STUDENTS STAFF LIBRARY ALUMNI NEWS & EVENTS SHOP DONATE YOUR UNI STUDY RESEARCH YOUR UNI Who We Are Our Purpose History Learning & Teaching Rankings & Achievements Faculty & Schools Academic Integrity Campuses CASTL Schools Engagement Venue & Facility Hire STUDENT LIFE Support Services Accommodation Spiritual Life Service Opportunities Student Associations Sport & Fitness FOLLOW US ONLINE COURSES Nursing Teaching Business Ministry Arts Counselling Lifestyle Medicine Science & Mathematics Postgraduate Courses Higher Degrees by Research Vocational Education Training Short Courses NEW STUDENTS Apply Now Pathways Not sure what to study? Early Entry Fees & costs Scholarships International Students Units Offered Ace Lab RESEARCH AT AVONDALE Researcher Profiles Research Integrity & Ethics Strategy & Performance Research Training & Support RESEARCH CENTRES Christian Education Lifestyle Medicine & Health Scripture, Spirituality & Society PUBLICATIONS ACORA Reporting Your Publications TEACH Journal PARTNER ENTITIES EGW Research Centre Adventist Heritage Centre ENQUIRE NOW → Avondale » Learning and Teaching Support Officer Learning and Teaching Support Officer Cooranbong and Wahroonga, NSW Part-time or Full-time Avondale University is seeking Learning and Teaching Support Officers on either part-time or full-time fixed-term contracts until end of 2026. Travel may be required between the Lake Macquarie and Wahroonga campuses. Be challenged and imagine with us This exciting role involves supporting University staff in the development and delivery of courses as well as supporting Avondale’s students. What will you do? Some of the main duties will include: Provide on-demand troubleshooting and timely resolution of LMS support requests in collaboration with Tech Services and the Centre for the Advancement of Learning and Teaching (CASTL). Provide assistance for academic and support staff seeking to improve their skill with Avondale’s learning technologies by contributing to training sessions and the development of instructional resources. Undertake a range of operational and administrative tasks to assist staff & students, particularly equity group students, in the use of learning technologies including but not limited to the LMS, online classrooms, booking and appointment systems, and appropriate support tickets. Assist Learning Designers to support teaching staff in the appropriate and effective day-to-day use of learning technologies in accordance with learning and teaching standards. Collaborate and communicate with student support services and academic staff to ensure effective and appropriate holistic support for students, especially students-at-risk. Ensure consistent application of policies, procedures, and service standards in all communications. Maintain confidentiality and exercise discretion when handling sensitive information. Maintain accurate records of activities and outcomes. Participate in continuous improvement processes to identify gaps and opportunities for refining university practice. Provide input and advice into relevant policies and procedures. About you To be successful in the Learning and Teaching Support Officer role, you will be a dynamic and responsive team player committed to providing guidance and support for Univeristy staff and students across a range of systems. Essential criteria A willingness to strongly support the mission, values, and ethos of Avondale. Completion of a relevant bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and education/training. Proven experience in providing learning technology support and development in a higher education setting. Demonstrated ability to learn and adopt digital tools to a high standard, and to deliver training in the use of learning technologies. Proficiency in learning technologies including CANVAS, CANVAS Studio, Turnitin, Microsoft Office 365, and Zoom. Commitment to high-quality customer service, including providing advice and support using a variety of communication platforms. Cooperate with all work health and safety policies and procedures related to the work being undertaken and ensure that their actions or omissions do not impact on the health and safety of others at Avondale.  Promote a safe workplace and identify unsafe practices. Understand and support equal opportunity principles. Desirable criteria Knowledge of pedagogical modes and practices, and experience supporting staff and students in the adoption of technology into their Learning & Teaching. Familiarity with Avondale University policies, procedures, or student administration systems. Understanding of the student lifecycle, student management systems, curriculum management systems, and common course-related processes. Please visit www.avondale.edu.au/employment for the job description and details of this position. For further information about the role, please email Avondale University’s People and Culture Manager at jolisa.rabo@avondale.edu.au . Email your application to employment@avondale.edu.au , including: A resume (four-page maximum) A statement addressing the selection criteria Contact details of three referees Applications close on 11 September 2026 Please note that we will be conducting interviews as applications come in, so please do not delay in submitting your application. Salary: Negotiable based on qualifications and experience. Applicants must have the right to work in Australia. Avondale is an equal opportunity employer and reserves the right to make a delayed appointment, not appoint, or appoint by invitation. Download Job Description ASK A QUESTION LIVE CHAT CALL Ask a question \" * \" indicates required fields Student type: * Select... Domestic (Australia or New Zealand) International Personal Details Your Name * First Name Family Name/Surname: Mobile Phone Number: * Emai